! MCP INITIALIZATION, printed p.72 (MCP_Mar63_001-249 PDF p.79) --
! MACHINE CONFIGURATION CHANGE: ADJUST THE NECESSARY TABLES.
!
! Fifty-six lines, forty-nine of which compile -- the densest page
! of the ASSIGN program so far.  Two boxed headings, and the first
! is the page's whole subject:
!
!   lines  1-3   "MACHINE CONFIGURATION CHANGE /
!                 ADJUST THE NECESSARY TABLES"
!   lines 52-54  "SAVE THE VALUES OF THE UNIT COUNT INDEX"
!
! >>> LINE 4 IS T ASIGN'S FORWARD BRANCH, AND THE BOOT RUN HAS BEEN
! STOPPING ON IT. <<<
!
! printed p.65 line 9 is "BZXVZ,T A9" commented "-IF A MACH CNF
! CHANGE", and the PC trail has ended at 004215.00 ever since p.65
! landed.  LINE 4 IS THAT ADDRESS, and the heading three lines above
! it names what it is for.  So the fixture's machine DOES report a
! configuration change, and this is the path it takes.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> A MULTIPLY, AND IT IS THE FIRST IN THIS CORPUS <<<
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Line 19 is
!
!     *(BU,24),T COMBO,40      -COMPUTE LOC WITHIN TABLE
!
! -- the OPERATION is a bare asterisk.  No page this project has
! read spells a multiply at all until now.  It compiles
! 003650.00 80  030024.21 90, and line 26's "M+,T DISK(T IXG)"
! compiles 003652.00 88  010000.20 90 -- THE SAME OPCODE BYTE, 90,
! differing in bit 23 of the second group (".21" against ".20").
! So multiply and add-to-memory share a byte and are told apart by
! one bit, which is the same shape the written minus has.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> AND A FIFTH WRITTEN MINUS, TWO LINES BELOW THE MULTIPLY <<<
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Line 20 is "-(BU,24),T 2COMB,20" compiling 003650.40 80
! 030012.30 10.  Its ".30" is the negative-sign modifier, exactly as
! on printed p.69 line 48 and p.70 lines 37 and 40.
!
! THE COUNT WAS ONE UNTIL TWO DAYS AGO.  MCP printed p.18 line 35
! was the only written minus in the corpus, and it is the row that
! found fieldToSM returning sign 0 for every unsigned field --
! every unsigned subtract in the model was an addition.  p.69 made
! it two, p.70 made it four, and this makes FIVE, on four pages.
!
! AND THE PAIR ON LINES 19-20 IS THE SHARPEST YET, because the
! operand of each is the OTHER HALF of one constant: printed p.63
! line 21 is "T COMBO VF,T TYBC+T MACBC+T REQBC" and line 22 is
! "T 2COMB VF,T TYBC+T MACBC".  Multiply by the three-field width,
! subtract the two-field width.  The two rows are a computation,
! and getting the minus wrong would have computed a different
! table offset silently.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! "V+" IS B0, FOR THE THIRD TIME
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Lines 40 and 48 are "V+,T IXG,S XCHAN" compiling 002152.20 B0.
! printed p.55 line 40 was transcribed as 80 and corrected to B0 at
! 1800 dpi (listing_typography.md 11); five rows on earlier pages
! already printed B0 for V+.  These two are a third page saying it,
! and they read cleanly at 900 dpi.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! TWO IMMEDIATE VALUES THAT PROVE THEIR OWN FIELD POSITION
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Line 36 is "KFI(BU,4),2" compiling 100000.00 80 and line 44 is
! "KFI(BU,4),5" compiling 240000.00 80.  A four-bit immediate
! LEFT-JUSTIFIED in the eighteen-bit address field is the value
! times 2^14: 2 x 16384 = 0o100000 and 5 x 16384 = 0o240000.  The
! two rows differ only in the value and the printed octal scales
! exactly.
!
! The comments say what they are looking for: "-LOOK FOR CONSOLE"
! and "-LOOK FOR A PRINTER", equipment codes 2 and 5 -- which is
! printed p.64's REQUEST VALIDITY CHECK TABLE read back.  That
! table's eight rows are DISK 1, CONSOLE 2, CARD READER 3, PUNCH 4,
! PRINTER 5, IQS 6, EXTRA 7, TAPE 10 octal.
!
! ONE NEW MNEMONIC: "SF" on lines 42 and 50, compiling 021027.12 F0
! against operands S YCOCH+.2 and S YPRCH+.2.  Written as printed.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> AND A SIXTH dds FROM A `DD` LABEL -- THIS ONE FROM AN
! ENTRY-MODE DD <<<
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Line 26 is "M+,T DISK(T IXG)" with NOTHING written, and it
! compiles 010000.20 90 -- 010000/512 = 8, so the length is EIGHT.
! T DISK is not a SYN: printed p.64 line 6 defines it as
!
!     T DISK  (8)DD(BU,8),1,1,0
!
! the first row of the REQUEST VALIDITY CHECK TABLE, an OCTAL
! entry-mode DD.  printed pp.66, 67 and 69 found this shape on
! plain "DD(BU,1),0" labels; this is the first time the dds comes
! from a DD that also carries an ENTRY MODE, and it carries
! identically.
!
! THE DECK HAD IT WRONG FIRST.  T DISK was written "SYN,(8)3652.0"
! with no dds and line 26 compiled 000000 for 010000 -- the single
! row that failed on this page.
!
! FOUR LISTING MARKS: lines 7, 23, 35 and 55.

        SLC, (8)4215.0

! ---- index names, printed p.61 ------------------------------------
TX1BR   SYN, $1
TIXF    SYN, $10
TIXG    SYN, $8
TIXH    SYN, $2
! ---- words, printed pp.61-71 --------------------------------------
TLUCT   SYN(BU,18), (8)3273.0
TCHSXW  SYN, (8)2152.0
TTYARA  SYN, (8)3647.0
TCOMBO  SYN, (8)3650.0
T2COMB  SYN, (8)3650.40
TDISK   SYN(BU,8), (8)3652.0
TMUCTX  SYN, (8)3655.0
TRCHSC  SYN, (8)3660.0
! ---- table offsets, printed pp.62-64 ------------------------------
TMCAD   SYN(BU,8), 0.8
TCHCNT  SYN(BU,4), 0.20
TCHAVL  SYN(BU,1), 0.25
TMULTI  SYN(BU,1), 0.27
TUNAVL  SYN(BU,1), 0.28
TUNASG  SYN(BU,1), 0.29
TCHOWN  SYN(BU,1), 0.32
TEQUIP  SYN(BU,4), 0.52
TUNITK  SYN(BU,4), 0.59
TUNRES  SYN(BU,1), 0.62
! ---- new on this page ---------------------------------------------
SXCHAN  SYN, (8)2152.0
SBAMCP  SYN, (8)2153.0
SYCOCH  SYN, (8)2156.0
SYPRCH  SYN, (8)2156.40
TDSIO   SYN, (8)4767.0
! ---- forward, onto printed p.73 and after -------------------------
TA9D    SYN, (8)4275.40
TA1C    SYN, (8)4320.0
TM      SYN, (8)4422.0

        SLC, (8)4215.0

! ---- MACHINE CONFIGURATION CHANGE / ADJUST THE NECESSARY TABLES ---
TA9     LX, TIXF, TCHSXW             ! line 4  -BEGINNING OF CHAN
                                      !           STAT TABLE
        CM0000(BU,24), 0.0($15)      ! line 5  -CLEAR CON FIG CHANGE
        LV, TIXG, SBAMCP             ! line 6  -SET UP THE DUMMY
                                      !           SIOL FOR
        TI, 1, TDSIO, 03.(TIXG)      ! line 7  -UNLOADING TAPES ON
                                      !           UNITS
        TI, 1, TDSIO+1., 9.(TIXG)    ! line 8  -FOR UNLOADING
                                      !           SCRATCH TAPES
        LX, TIXG, TTYARA             ! line 9  -CLEAR THE MACHINE
                                      !           CONFIGUATION
TCM9    CM0000, TMCAD(TIXG)          ! line 10 -COUNT TABLE
        V+C, TIXG, TCOMBO            ! line 11
        BZXCZ, TCM9                  ! line 12
        CM0000, TLUCT                ! line 14 -CLEAR LARGEST COUNT
                                      !           AREA
        LX, TIXH, TMUCTX             ! line 15 -BEGINNING OF THE
                                      !           MULTI UNIT CNT TBLE
TA9A    CM0000, TCHCNT(TIXH)         ! line 16 -CLEAR THE UNIT COUNT
                                      !           AREA
        L, TEQUIP(TIXF), 40          ! line 17 -GET EQUIP FOR MACH
                                      !           CONF
        BRZ, TB9B                    ! line 18 -IF NO EQUIP ON THIS
                                      !           CHAN
        *(BU,24), TCOMBO, 40         ! line 19 -COMPUTE LOC WITHIN
                                      !           TABLE
        -(BU,24), T2COMB, 20         ! line 20
        L(BU,64), $R, 20             ! line 21 -LEFT SHIFT TO VF
        LV, TIXG, $R                 ! line 22
        LI(BU,1), 1                  ! line 23 -AT LEAST GIVE A
                                      !           COUNT OF ONE
        BZB, TEQUIP(TIXF), T9M       ! line 24 -IF A NON TAPE CHAN
        L, TUNITK(TIXF)              ! line 25 -GET COUNT FOR MULTI
                                      !           CHAN
T9M     M+, TDISK(TIXG)              ! line 26 -ADD CONFIGURATION TO
                                      !           TABLE
        BB, TMULTI(TIXF), TA9D       ! line 27 -IF A MULTI CHANNEL
        BB, TCHAVL(TIXF), TA9B       ! line 28 -IF CHANNEL NOT
                                      !           AVAILABLE
        BB, TCHOWN(TIXF), TA9BA      ! line 29 -IF MCP LEVEL IT IS
                                      !           NOT AVAIL TO PP
        BZB, TUNAVL(TIXF), TB9       ! line 30 -IF UNIT IS AVAILABLE
TA9B    BZB, TUNASG(TIXF), TM        ! line 31 -IF THE UNIT IS
                                      !           ASSIGNED
TA9BA   LVI, TX1BR, TB9              ! line 32 -LOAD FOR SUB ROUTINE
                                      !           BRANCH
        CT0011(BU,2), TUNRES(TIXF)   ! line 33 -IS UNIT RESERVED BY PP
        BZRZ, TA1C                   ! line 34 -YES
TB9     LF, TEQUIP(TIXF)             ! line 35
        KFI(BU,4), 2                 ! line 36 -LOOK FOR CONSOLE
        BZAE, TB9A                   ! line 37 -NO
        LV, TIXG, TIXF               ! line 38
        CM1111(BU,1), TIXG+.24       ! line 39 -SET IX NEG SO TO SUB
        V+, TIXG, SXCHAN             ! line 40 -COMPUTE CONSOLE
                                      !           CHANNEL
        SV, TIXG, $R                 ! line 41
        SF(BU,17), SYCOCH+.2, 46     ! line 42
        B, TB9B                      ! line 43
TB9A    KFI(BU,4), 5                 ! line 44 -LOOK FOR A PRINTER
        BZAE, TB9B                   ! line 45 -NO
        LV, TIXG, TIXF               ! line 46
        CM1111(BU,1), TIXG+.24       ! line 47 -SET IX NEG SO TO SUB
        V+, TIXG, SXCHAN             ! line 48 -COMPUTE THE PRINTER
                                      !           CHANNEL
        SV, TIXG, $R                 ! line 49
        SF(BU,17), SYPRCH+.2, 46     ! line 50
TB9B    CB+, TIXF, TA9A              ! line 51

! ---- SAVE THE VALUES OF THE UNIT COUNT INDEX ----------------------
        V-I, TIXH, 0.32              ! line 55 -REDUCE BY A HALF
        SX, TIXH, TRCHSC             ! line 56
        END, TA9

